<title>CANADA: Revenue Canada confirms dumping of Chinese garlic.</title>
<headline>Revenue Canada confirms dumping of Chinese garlic.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Revenue Canada on Wednesday confirmed that fresh garlic imported from China was dumped in Canada at an average of 70 percent below fairly traded prices.</p>
<p>Canada's International Trade Tribunal will begin public hearings on the case on February 20 and a decision is expected by March 21.</p>
<p>If the tribunal agrees with the Revenue Canada ruling, the provisional anti-dumping duties that the agency has been collecting since last November will remain in place.</p>
<p>The government agency had started an investigation last August, following complaints from the Garlic Growers Association of Ontario, which alleged that dumping of cheap garlic was hurting their industry. It made a preliminary decision last November.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau, 613-235-6745))</p>
